# PART 1 — Jenkins Installation

---

## Option A — Docker par install (fastest, local/dev)

```bash
# Jenkins official image run karo
docker run -d \
  --name jenkins \
  -p 8080:8080 \
  -p 50000:50000 \
  -v jenkins_home:/var/jenkins_home \
  -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock \
  jenkins/jenkins:lts

# Initial admin password lao
docker exec jenkins cat /var/jenkins_home/secrets/initialAdminPassword
```

> 💡 `/var/run/docker.sock` mount karna zaroori hai taaki Jenkins andar se Docker commands chala sake.

---

## Option B — EC2 (Ubuntu) par install (production)

```bash
# Step 1: Java install karo (Jenkins ko Java chahiye)
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y fontconfig openjdk-17-jre
java -version   # verify

# Step 2: Jenkins repo add karo
sudo wget -O /usr/share/keyrings/jenkins-keyring.asc \
  https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable/jenkins.io-2023.key

echo "deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/jenkins-keyring.asc]" \
  https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable binary/ | \
  sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/jenkins.list > /dev/null

# Step 3: Install Jenkins
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y jenkins

# Step 4: Start and enable
sudo systemctl start jenkins
sudo systemctl enable jenkins
sudo systemctl status jenkins

# Step 5: Initial password
sudo cat /var/lib/jenkins/secrets/initialAdminPassword
```

Access karo: `http://<EC2-IP>:8080`

**EC2 Security Group mein port 8080 open karo (inbound rule add karo).**

