# PART 8 — Shared Libraries (Code Reuse)

---

Agar multiple pipelines mein same code likhte ho (ECR login, Slack notify, etc.) → Shared Library mein rakh do.

### Setup

```
GitHub repo structure:
  jenkins-shared-library/
  └── vars/
      ├── ecrLogin.groovy
      ├── helmDeploy.groovy
      └── slackNotify.groovy
```

```groovy
// vars/ecrLogin.groovy
def call(String region, String registry) {
    sh """
        aws ecr get-login-password --region ${region} | \
        docker login --username AWS --password-stdin ${registry}
    """
}
```

```groovy
// vars/slackNotify.groovy
def call(String status, String appName, String buildNum) {
    def color = status == 'SUCCESS' ? 'good' : 'danger'
    def emoji = status == 'SUCCESS' ? '✅' : '❌'
    slackSend(
        color: color,
        message: "${emoji} *${appName}* build #${buildNum}: ${status}"
    )
}
```

**Jenkins mein register karo:**
```
Manage Jenkins → System → Global Pipeline Libraries
Name    : my-shared-lib
Default version: main
Source  : Git → https://github.com/myorg/jenkins-shared-library.git
```

**Use karo Jenkinsfile mein:**
```groovy
@Library('my-shared-lib') _

pipeline {
    stages {
        stage('Push to ECR') {
            steps {
                ecrLogin('ap-south-1', '123456789.dkr.ecr.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com')
                sh 'docker push my-app:latest'
            }
        }
    }
    post {
        always {
            slackNotify(currentBuild.result, 'my-app', env.BUILD_NUMBER)
        }
    }
}
```

