# PART 10 — Troubleshooting Jenkins

---

| Problem | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| `Permission denied` running docker | Jenkins user ko docker group mein add karo: `sudo usermod -aG docker jenkins` |
| `git: authentication failed` | GitHub credentials Jenkins mein update karo |
| Build stuck / hanging | Timeout option add karo: `timeout(time: 30, unit: 'MINUTES')` |
| `No space left on device` | `docker system prune -f` + old workspaces clean karo |
| Webhook not triggering | Jenkins URL publicly accessible hai? Firewall port 8080 open hai? |
| `CSRF missing` | Manage Jenkins → Security → CSRF → Enable proxy compatibility |
| Plugin conflict | Safe restart karo: `http://jenkins:8080/safeRestart` |
| Pipeline not finding Jenkinsfile | Repo root mein `Jenkinsfile` (capital J) hona chahiye |
| OOMKilled Jenkins pod (K8s) | memory limits badhaao values.yaml mein |
| Slave agent not connecting | SSH credentials check karo, Java version match honi chahiye |

### Useful Jenkins URLs
```
http://jenkins:8080/restart           # restart
http://jenkins:8080/safeRestart       # wait for builds to finish then restart
http://jenkins:8080/systemInfo        # system info
http://jenkins:8080/log/all           # all logs
http://jenkins:8080/script            # Groovy script console (admin only)
```

### Groovy Console — Emergency fixes
```groovy
// Stuck build cancel karo
Jenkins.instance.queue.items.each { it.cancel() }

// All running builds abort karo
Jenkins.instance.items.each { job ->
  job.builds.each { build ->
    if (build.isBuilding()) build.doStop()
  }
}
```

