## Interviewer Deep-Dive Questions — aur unke answers

**Q: "ALB (Application Load Balancer) aur NLB (Network Load Balancer) mein kya difference hai? Tumne ALB kyun choose kiya?"**
> "ALB (Application Load Balancer) Layer 7 par kaam karta hai — HTTP/HTTPS, path-based routing, host-based routing support karta hai. NLB (Network Load Balancer) Layer 4 par kaam karta hai — TCP (Transmission Control Protocol)/UDP (User Datagram Protocol), bahut fast hai lekin sirf IP+port se route karta hai, content nahi dekhta. Microservices ke liye ALB perfect hai kyunki ek ALB se multiple services route kar sakte hain path ke basis par."

**Q: "CNAME (Canonical Name record) ki jagah Alias record kyun?"**
> "CNAME root domain par nahi chalta — `mycompany.com` par CNAME nahi laga sakte, sirf subdomains par. Alias AWS-specific feature hai jo root domain par bhi kaam karta hai. Plus Alias records free hain aur faster resolve hote hain kyunki AWS internally handle karta hai."

**Q: "SSL (Secure Sockets Layer) termination ALB (Application Load Balancer) par kyun, pods par kyun nahi?"**
> "ALB par terminate karne se pods ko SSL handle nahi karna padta — simple HTTP chalaate hain. Certificate ek jagah manage hota hai. ACM auto-renew karta hai certificates. Agar har pod SSL handle kare toh certificate management complex ho jaata hai."

**Q: "Zero downtime deploy kaise ensure karte ho?"**
> "Helm ka default rolling update strategy use karta hoon. `maxUnavailable: 0` aur `maxSurge: 1` set karta hoon — matlab pehle naya pod start hota hai, healthy hone par hi purana terminate hota hai. Readiness probe ensure karta hai ki pod traffic lene ke liye ready hai tab hi Service mein add hota hai."

**Q: "Agar Route 53 record galat ho jaaye toh?"**
> "TTL kam hone ki wajah se DNS propagation fast hoti hai. Galat record fix karo → 60 seconds mein propagate. Plus health check Route 53 mein laga sakte hain — agar ALB unhealthy ho toh automatically failover ho jaata hai dusre region ya backup endpoint par."

